// THE CREDENTIAL STORE CARRIES THE INSTANCE ROOT ITS CURSOR RUNTIME ROOT IS DERIVED UNDER, so the records a
// recovery reads and the directory it observes and removes cannot come from two instances: a store re-spelled
// with store A's slots and another root B is a forged literal, and neither recovery nor the seal accepts a root
// beside the store. The positive control is the same two calls through the store alone.
test fn a_credential_store_pairing_one_stores_slots_with_another_root_is_refused_at_compile() -> ProcessExit {
  census_exit(census_verdict(census: seal_violations(source: credential_store_ab_source, subject: "CredentialAcquisitionStore"), holds: fn(n) { n == 1 }))
}

